summary:
Re-judgement after one fix round.
(1) CP-4 delivers AC-8 and D-20:
- supporter houses (roof fan flag) and parked vehicles are the only things mobs ignite;
- each fire blocks its footprint plus one ring for exactly 600 ticks, then frees it and leaves the prop charred;
- flow fields route around fires;
- townspeople within 140 px flee a new fire and supporters within 56 px leave the crowd;
- bodies caught in a new ring are moved to the nearest open tile.
(2) Tests: T-13 and T-14 are unchanged. The new test/arson-extra.test.js covers eviction, D-20 and mid-burn determinism, and reviewers showed by mutation that each one bites.
(3) No gaming: npm test (61), e2e (3) and design_check are green.
(4) Accepted minors and nits:
- render fire paths have no automated test (my headless run after the rename showed 2 fires burning and 0 page errors);
- the commented  alias stays until locked arson.test.js is next unlocked;
- smoke only at 'hi' quality (documented);
- the bike colour change;
- release and backup eviction paths are untested.
(5) The scope-creep finding is overruled by D-20 (from the user-approved plan). Content line holds.
(6) Ready.
